{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pulls/14","id":4772438838,"node_id":"PR_kwDOS2MamM8AAAABHHWjNg","html_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pull/14","diff_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pull/14.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pull/14.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/issues/14","number":14,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Propose s-core_sw_fabric engineering workflow pilot","user":{"login":"jnsagai","id":20442122,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNDQyMTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20442122?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai","html_url":"https://github.com/jnsagai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnsagai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The existing `s-core_sw_fabric` implementation provides engineering workflow orchestration, source-bound traceability, bounded agent context, deterministic assessment, and portable review evidence. This PR proposes a small Hephaestus pilot and makes the candidate discoverable from the tooling catalog and documentation.\n\nThe implementation baseline is [7e24a43](https://github.com/jnsagai/s-core_sw_fabric/tree/7e24a43c258f1dcaa2b27e02b501964847bc8714). The proposal maps it to Hephaestus's scope, describes component authority and integration with the current ubcode/Pharaoh workflow, links architecture and acceptance records, and defines a first adapter/example/negative-test pilot. Retained fixture results, historical measurements, and human engineering acceptance remain distinct.\n\nMaintainer feedback requested on the pilot's target repository, metamodel/runtime boundary, ownership, dependency review, and acceptance checks. This PR contributes the proposal; implementation import and qualification remain pending.\n\nRelated: #11 (website content aligned with project scope). This does not close the broader content review issue.\n\nValidation:\n- Hugo Extended 0.163.0: `hugo --gc --minify` passed using the pinned theme submodule.\n- Hugo inventory and shared navigation generation passed.\n- Sphinx 8.2.3 / Sphinx-Needs 8.5.0: `python -m sphinx -b html docs public/docs -W` passed on the final source.\n- All 16 implementation/evidence references resolve to tracked paths at the pinned implementation commit; proposal rendering, tooling-to-docs URL, and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nThree documentation files changed. Existing implementation/native test suites were not rerun because this PR changes documentation only. The new page carries the repository's Apache-2.0 header, and the single commit includes Signed-off-by and Assisted-by trailers.\n\nAssisted-by: Codex\n","created_at":"2026-10-07T12:12:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T12:21:14Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c6207774c862cb6b8b6f05b74870e577a19417b4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pulls/14/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pulls/14/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaestus/hephaestus/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eclipse-hephaest